# The app image is built from the repository root (see app/Dockerfile) so that the
# server and the sibling `cli/` module can both go in. That means the default build
# context is the whole repo, most of which the image has no use for — so this file
# is an allowlist rather than the usual short list of exclusions.
#
# Everything is excluded, then what the Dockerfile actually copies from is let
# back in.
*

!app/
!cli/

# The runtime image also ships the images/ Dockerfiles so a missing extra image can
# be built from the web interface. Only the Dockerfiles — nothing else in there is
# needed, since each one is its own whole build context.
!images/*.Dockerfile

# ...minus what must never be sent even from those.
app/web/node_modules
app/web/dist
app/web/.smoke
app/*.db
app/*.db-*
app/dbcanvas
app/testdata
**/*.log
.env
